    "title": "Theme — Chitchat",
    "text": "Skip to content\nChitchat\nPractice studio\n\nCHITCHAT / DESIGN LIBRARY\n\nThe little things, together.\n\nOur colors, controls, and conversation pieces. A living picture of how Chitchat looks and feels.\n\npick something. press things. see how it feels.\n\nDark appearance\nFoundations\nButtons\nSelection\nAvatars\nVoice\nForms\nChat\nFeedback\nFoundations\n\nThe shared palette and type styles behind the studio.\n\nbackground\n\ncard\n\nforeground\n\nprimary\n\nsecondary\n\nmuted\n\nmuted-foreground\n\nborder\n\ndestructive\n\nsuccess\n\ninfo\n\nwarning\n\nHeading · 30 px / Geist\n\nA little hello.\n\nBody · 16 px / Geist\n\nSmall talk gets easier with a little practice. Start wherever you feel comfortable.\n\nAnnotation · Shantell Sans\n\nmake it your own\n\nButtons\n\nComfortable app controls: 48 px standard buttons, 52 px main actions, and at least 44 px for compact controls.\n\ndefault\nContinue\nDisabled\nsecondary\nContinue\nDisabled\noutline\nContinue\nDisabled\nghost\nContinue\nDisabled\ndestructive\nContinue\nDisabled\nlink\nContinue\nDisabled\n14 px label\nCompact · 44 px\n15 px label\nSmall · 44 px\n16 px label\nDefault · 48 px\n18 px label\nLarge · 52 px\nConnecting…\nSelect place\nTry any enabled button.\nChevronLeft\nChevronRight\nArrowRight\nCheck\nPlus\nX\nShuffle\nSparkles\nMic\nMicOff\nPhoneOff\nVolume2\nSelection\n\nThe studio’s place picker, selection button, chevrons, and illustrated scenes. Browse the places and open a photo.\n\nPlace picker · browse and select\nPlace\nneighborhood cafe\n\nA cozy cafe with warm coffee, window seats, and a gentle hum of conversation.\n\nSelect place\nTry the chevrons or arrow keys.\nImage collection · press to enlarge\nRestaurant\nAirport\nCoworking Lounge\nRooftop Terrace\nAvatars\n\nOur practice partners, with the shared 56 px avatar and selected ring. Choose one to compare states.\n\nAlex\nJamie\nDani\nFelix\nVera\nLily\nVoice\n\nThe circular talk control, Chit’s animated icon, and audio waveforms. These are visual previews; they don’t access your microphone or start a conversation.\n\nTalk button · 56 px\nPress to talk\nChit · voice states\nIdle\nListening\nThinking\nSpeaking\nSimulated audio level · 50%\nLive conversations use actual audio loudness.\nWaveform · resting / processing\nWatercolor · listening with you\nI’m listening\nQuiet\nSpeaking\nMuted\n\nSwitch from Speaking to Quiet to watch the paint settle. This preview uses simulated speech.\n\nSimulated loudness · 65%\nForms\n\nLanguage, conversation mode, and text inputs with their help, error, and disabled states.\n\nPreferences\nPractice language\nArabic\nChinese\nDanish\nDutch\nEnglish\nFilipino\nFrench\nGerman\nGreek\nHebrew\nHindi\nIndonesian\nItalian\nJapanese\nKorean\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nRussian\nSpanish\nSwedish\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nVietnamese\nConversation mode\nFree talk\nGuided\n\nSpeak freely. Ask for a suggested reply whenever you need one.\n\nText fields\nYour backstory\n\nHow do you know each other? What brings you here?\n\nError state\nDescribe your scene before continuing.\nChat\n\nA little room to talk. A conversation thread and a spacious input with its controls tucked below.\n\nChit:\nHey, I’m Chit. What would you like to feel more confident talking about?\n\nPreview only · Enter to send, Shift + Enter for a new line.\nFeedback\n\nStatus badges, notices, cards, and the conversation bubbles you see during practice.\n\ndefault\nsecondary\noutline\nsuccess-light\nwarning-light\ndestructive-light\ninfo-light\nprimary-light\ninvert-light\nfocus-light\ninfo\nsuccess\nwarning\ndestructive\ninvert\nfocus\nprimary-outline\ninfo-outline\nsuccess-outline\nwarning-outline\ndestructive-outline\ninvert-outline\nfocus-outline\nYou’re ready\nYour scene is set. Take your time.\nConnection interrupted\nTake a breath and try again when you’re ready.\nA little progress\nEvery conversation counts.\nYou made an introduction and kept the conversation going.\n\nAlex:\nHey! Is this seat taken?\n\nYou:\nNot at all. Go ahead!\n\nA\n\nAlex:\nThanks! Do you come here often?\n\nA little practice goes a long way.\nChitchat",
